---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'; import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro'; import { timeline } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="The professional story of Shorif Ahmmed: a self-taught garment pattern maker progressing from digitizing and grading to development work.">
  <section class="page-hero shell"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>A finance graduate who found his craft in <em>pattern precision.</em></h1><p class="lead narrow">I entered garments in 2022 without a textile degree or formal pattern-making course. I learned by doing: digitizing senior pattern masters’ hard patterns, grading existing work, studying corrections and gradually taking on development responsibility.</p></section>
  <section class="shell split section-space"><div><SectionHead eyebrow="Professional story" title="Progress built through observation, repetition and responsibility." /></div><div class="prose"><p>My BBA in Finance & Banking did not provide a conventional route into apparel. Pattern making became the place where structured thinking and practical making met. Gerber AccuMark gave me a working language: points, curves, balance, measurements and controlled change.</p><p>Today I work in the Sample department at Intercept Shirt Manufacturing Limited, part of VLR Tex Group. My work focuses on woven development—particularly shirts and overshirts—through the full sample feedback loop.</p><p>I do not present myself as a finished garment technologist. My direction is to earn that depth through stronger construction, fit, fabric and production knowledge, supported by evidence and consistent documentation.</p></div></section>
  <section class="dark-section timeline-section"><div class="shell"><SectionHead eyebrow="Career journey" title="From CAD support to pattern responsibility." /> <div class="timeline">{timeline.map((x) => <article><time>{x.period}</time><div><h3>{x.role}</h3><p>{x.org}</p><small>{x.note}</small></div></article>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="shell section-space values"><SectionHead eyebrow="Operating values" title="How I want the work to be judged." /><div class="capability-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Accuracy over theatre</h3><p>Claims should be specific, supportable and clear about their limits.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Learning in public</h3><p>Documenting the path from observation to stronger technical judgment.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Confidentiality by design</h3><p>Sharing methods and lessons without exposing commercial source material.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Systems thinking</h3><p>Connecting pattern, fabric, construction, fit and feedback as one system.</p></article></div></section>
</Base>
